@startuml process-view
' 4+1 — PROCESS VIEW: runtime concurrency, the 3-slot gate, and per-run processes.
title 4+1 Process View — concurrency & synchronization (gate = 3)

|CLI invocations|
start
:./implement-issue.ps1 --issueid N;
:dedup + create Secret;
:argo submit;

|Argo controller|
if (running Workflows < 3?) then (yes)
  :admit Workflow\n(acquire semaphore slot);
else (no)
  :enqueue\n(block on semaphore);
  :... wait for a slot ...;
  :admit when freed;
endif

|Workflow pod (per issue, up to 3 in parallel)|
fork
  :init: git clone (own emptyDir);
  fork
    :main: agent-entrypoint.ps1;
    :run coding agent (LLM I/O);
    :quality gates;
    :push + open PR;
  fork again
    :sidecar: mssql (localhost:1433);
  end fork
  :main exits -> sidecar killed;
end fork
:release semaphore slot;

|Argo controller|
:next queued Workflow admitted;
stop

note right
Up to 3 pods run truly in parallel.
Each pod is a separate process group with
its own PID namespace, network namespace,
DB, and secret — no shared mutable state.
end note

@enduml
